/* ---------------- learn cards ---------------- */
const LEARN = [
 {sec:"1 · What is a life cycle? 什么是生命周期"},
 {t:"Life cycle 生命周期", pics:["hen","chick","henegg"], facts:[
  "A <b>life cycle</b> is the <b>stages</b> a living thing goes through, from the start of its life until it becomes an <b>adult</b> that can <b>reproduce</b>.",
  "Then the cycle starts again: the adult makes <b>young (or seeds) of its own kind</b>.",
  "Living things reproduce so that <b>their own kind will continue to exist</b> and not die out.",
  "Different living things have different life cycles, and different <b>life spans</b> (how long they live): a housefly lives a few weeks, a dog about 10 to 15 years, many people 80 years or more, and some trees hundreds of years."],
  zh:"生命周期 = 从生命开始到长成能繁殖的成体所经过的各个阶段，然后重新开始。寿命长短因生物而不同。",
  trap:"⚠️ A life cycle is not just \"growing bigger\". It ends with an adult that reproduces, so the cycle goes round again."},
 {sec:"2 · Plants 植物的生命周期"},
 {t:"Life cycle of a flowering plant 开花植物", pics:["beanstages","seedlings"], ch:"plantcyc", facts:[
  "<b>seed → germinating seed → seedling → young plant → adult plant</b> (flowers, fruits) → seeds again.",
  "<b>Germination</b> is when a seed starts to grow. The <b>root grows out first</b>, then the <b>shoot</b> grows upwards.",
  "A <b>seedling</b> is a very young plant with its first green leaves.",
  "The adult plant produces <b>flowers</b>. Flowers develop into <b>fruits</b>, and the fruits contain <b>seeds</b>. Each seed can grow into a new plant.",
  "Green bean and balsam plants finish their life cycle in a few months; a mango tree takes years before it bears fruits."],
  zh:"种子 → 发芽 → 幼苗 → 小植物 → 成株（开花结果）→ 种子。发芽时先长根，再长芽。",
  trap:"⚠️ The ROOT comes out first, then the shoot. A seed is living even when it is not growing yet."},
 {t:"Inside a seed 种子里面有什么", ch:"seedparts", facts:[
  "<b>A — seed coat</b>: the outer covering. It <b>protects</b> the parts inside.",
  "<b>B — seed leaf</b>: stores <b>food</b>. The young plant uses this food to grow until its <b>green leaves can make food</b>.",
  "<b>C — tiny young plant</b>: it has a tiny root and a tiny shoot. It grows into the seedling.",
  "As the stored food is used up, the seed leaves become <b>smaller</b>, <b>shrivel</b> and <b>drop off</b>."],
  zh:"种皮：保护。子叶：储存养分，供幼苗生长，直到绿叶能自己制造食物；养分用完，子叶会变小、干瘪、脱落。",
  trap:"⚠️ Seed leaves are NOT the same as the first green leaves. Seed leaves GIVE stored food; green leaves MAKE food."},
 {t:"What a seed needs to germinate 发芽的条件", pics:["beansprouts"], emo:["water","air","warm"], facts:[
  "A seed needs <b>water</b>, <b>air</b> and a <b>suitable temperature (warmth)</b> to germinate.",
  "It does <b>NOT</b> need <b>light</b>. Seeds germinate in a dark cupboard — bean sprouts (taugeh) are grown in the dark.",
  "It does <b>NOT</b> need <b>soil</b>. Seeds germinate on wet cotton wool or tissue paper. The food it needs is stored in its seed leaves.",
  "After germination, the <b>seedling needs light</b> to make food. A seedling kept in the dark grows tall, thin and yellow, and dies when the stored food is used up."],
  zh:"发芽三条件：水、空气、适宜的温度。不需要光，也不需要泥土。但发芽以后，幼苗需要光来制造食物。",
  trap:"⚠️ Light is NOT needed for germination, but it IS needed by the seedling later. Read carefully: \"germinate\" or \"grow well\"?"},
 {t:"Germination experiments 发芽实验", ch:"germ1", facts:[
  "Fair test: change only <b>ONE</b> condition and keep everything else the <b>same</b> (same kind and number of seeds, same amount of cotton wool and water).",
  "Dish A (wet) vs dish B (dry) → seeds need <b>water</b>.",
  "Dish D (warm, dark) vs dish C (cold, dark) → seeds need a <b>suitable temperature</b>.",
  "Dish A (light) vs dish D (dark) → both germinated, so <b>light is not needed</b>.",
  "Seeds under <b>boiled water that has cooled</b>, with a <b>layer of oil</b> on top, do not germinate: boiling removes the <b>air</b> in the water, and the oil stops air from getting back in.",
  "Use <b>several seeds</b> in each set-up: one seed may be damaged, so more seeds give a more <b>reliable</b> result."],
  zh:"每次只改变一个条件。煮过放凉的水 + 油层 = 没有空气。每组多放几颗种子，结果更可靠。",
  trap:"⚠️ Dish A and dish C are NOT a fair pair: they differ in temperature AND light. Compare C with D (both dark)."},
 {sec:"3 · Insects 昆虫的生命周期"},
 {t:"3 stages: egg → nymph → adult 三个阶段", pics:["roachnymph","hoppernymph","dfnymph"], emo:["cockroach"], ch:"cyc3", facts:[
  "Cockroaches, grasshoppers, crickets and dragonflies have a <b>3-stage</b> life cycle: <b>egg → nymph → adult</b>. (In the diagram: J egg case, K nymph, L adult.)",
  "A <b>nymph</b> looks like a small adult, but it has <b>no wings</b> yet.",
  "A nymph grows by <b>moulting</b>: it sheds its hard outer covering several times. The wings appear after the last moult.",
  "A cockroach lays its eggs in an <b>egg case</b>.",
  "A <b>dragonfly nymph lives in water</b> and does not look much like the adult. It is still a 3-stage life cycle — there is <b>no pupa</b>."],
  zh:"三阶段：卵 → 若虫 → 成虫。若虫像缩小的成虫，但没有翅膀，靠蜕皮长大。蜻蜓的若虫住在水里。",
  trap:"⚠️ No pupa = 3 stages. The young of a cockroach is a NYMPH, not a larva."},
 {t:"4 stages: egg → larva → pupa → adult 四个阶段", pics:["bfegg","bflarva","bfpupa","butterfly"], ch:"t4", facts:[
  "Butterflies, moths, mosquitoes, houseflies, beetles (ladybird, mealworm beetle), bees and ants have a <b>4-stage</b> life cycle.",
  "The <b>larva</b> looks very different from the adult. It <b>eats a lot</b> and <b>grows quickly</b>, moulting several times. Larvae: caterpillar, wriggler (mosquito), maggot (housefly), mealworm (beetle).",
  "The <b>pupa does not feed</b> and hardly moves, but it is <b>alive</b>: inside it, the body is changing into the adult. A butterfly pupa is a <b>chrysalis</b>.",
  "The <b>adult</b> reproduces: it lays eggs, and the cycle starts again.",
  "A butterfly lays its eggs on the <b>leaves the caterpillars will eat</b>, so the young have food as soon as they hatch."],
  zh:"四阶段：卵 → 幼虫 → 蛹 → 成虫。幼虫吃得多、长得快；蛹不吃东西、几乎不动，但还活着，身体正在变成成虫。",
  trap:"⚠️ The pupa is NOT dead. Its body is changing into the adult inside."},
 {t:"Mosquitoes and dengue 蚊子和骨痛热症", pics:["mozlarva","mozpupa","aedes"], facts:[
  "The <b>Aedes</b> mosquito spreads <b>dengue</b>. It lays its eggs in or near <b>stagnant (still) water</b>: flower-pot plates, pails, bamboo pole holders, blocked roof gutters, even a bottle cap of water.",
  "Its <b>larvae and pupae live in water</b>. They come up to the water surface to <b>take in air</b>.",
  "<b>Removing stagnant water</b> (turn over pails, empty plates, change the water in vases) means the larvae and pupae cannot develop into adults. This <b>breaks the life cycle</b>, so there are fewer mosquitoes.",
  "A thin layer of oil on water that cannot be emptied stops the larvae and pupae from getting air, so they die.",
  "A mosquito pupa does not feed, but it can still tumble about in the water."],
  zh:"去掉积水 → 蚊子不能产卵，幼虫和蛹不能在水里长成成虫 → 打断生命周期。",
  trap:"⚠️ Spraying kills only the adults that are already flying. Removing stagnant water stops NEW mosquitoes from developing."},
 {t:"Do the young look like the adults? 幼体像不像成体", pics:["chick","kitten","bflarva","maggot","mealworm","tadpole"], facts:[
  "Some young <b>look like their parents</b>, only smaller: chick, kitten, puppy, baby. Cockroach and grasshopper nymphs look like the adults too, but have no wings.",
  "Some young <b>do not look like their parents</b>: caterpillar (butterfly), maggot (housefly), wriggler (mosquito), mealworm (beetle), tadpole (frog). They change a lot as they grow.",
  "Young that look very different from the adult often live in a different place or eat different food (a tadpole lives in water; a frog lives on land and in water)."],
  zh:"小鸡、小猫、若虫像成体；毛毛虫、蛆、孑孓、面包虫、蝌蚪不像成体。",
  trap:"⚠️ A caterpillar is not a worm and a tadpole is not a fish — they are the young of a butterfly and a frog."},
 {sec:"4 · Frogs, chickens and humans 青蛙、鸡和人"},
 {t:"Life cycle of a frog 青蛙", pics:["frogspawn","tadpole","froglet","frog"], facts:[
  "<b>Egg</b>: frogs lay many eggs <b>in water</b>, covered in jelly (<b>frogspawn</b>).",
  "<b>Tadpole</b>: lives in water, swims with its <b>tail</b>, breathes through <b>gills</b>.",
  "<b>Froglet</b> (young frog): grows <b>back legs first, then front legs</b>; its tail becomes <b>shorter</b>; it starts to breathe through <b>lungs</b>.",
  "<b>Adult frog</b>: no tail; lives <b>on land and in water</b>; breathes through <b>lungs and moist skin</b>.",
  "Frog: egg → tadpole → froglet → adult frog. There is <b>no pupa</b>."],
  zh:"卵（在水里）→ 蝌蚪（鳃、尾巴）→ 幼蛙（先长后腿，再长前腿，尾巴变短）→ 成蛙（用肺和皮肤呼吸）。",
  trap:"⚠️ The BACK legs appear before the front legs. A tadpole cannot live out of water: it breathes through gills."},
 {t:"Chicken and humans 鸡和人", pics:["henegg","chick","hen"], emo:["baby"], facts:[
  "Chicken: <b>egg → chick → adult</b> (hen or rooster). The chick grows inside the egg and <b>hatches</b> after about <b>21 days</b>.",
  "A chick <b>looks like a small adult</b>; it is covered with soft, fluffy feathers.",
  "Human: <b>baby → child → teenager → adult</b>. A human baby grows inside its mother and is born alive.",
  "Cats and dogs also give birth to young alive. A kitten looks like a small cat."],
  zh:"鸡：蛋 → 小鸡 → 成鸡（约 21 天孵出）。人：婴儿 → 儿童 → 青少年 → 成人。",
  trap:"⚠️ Not every life cycle starts with an egg we can see: humans, cats and dogs give birth to young alive."},
 {sec:"5 · Exam skills 答题技巧"},
 {t:"Full-mark answers 怎样拿满分", ch:"insectmass", facts:[
  "Use the exact stage names: <b>egg, larva, pupa, nymph, adult</b>; <b>seed, seedling</b>; tadpole, froglet; chick.",
  "Germination: name <b>all three</b> conditions — <b>water, air, suitable temperature</b>.",
  "Graph of an insect's mass: it <b>increases quickly</b> in the larva stage (it eats a lot) and <b>remains the same</b> in the pupa stage (it <b>does not feed</b>). Write \"remains the same\", not just \"did not increase\".",
  "Seed leaves: say the young plant <b>used up the food stored</b> in them — not just \"they store food\".",
  "Dengue: say <b>remove stagnant water</b> so the larvae and pupae cannot develop into adults.",
  "Fair test: say what was <b>changed</b> and what was kept the <b>same</b>."],
  zh:"用准确的阶段名称；发芽三个条件都要写；蛹不吃东西所以质量不变；子叶变小是因为养分被用掉了。"}
];

